# Docs: Avatar photos in examples

When a docs demo or MDX fence needs a person/entity face, prefer a **real photo** via `src`. Do not stage fallback-only Avatars just to fill a row.

## Do

- Pass `src` with a stable portrait URL whenever the example shows people (assignees, teammates, account menus, AvatarGroup clusters)
- Reuse the shared mock portrait host already used in ViraUI preview blocks: `https://mockmind-api.uifaces.co/content/human/{n}.jpg` (vary `{n}` per person)
- Still pass required `fallback` (initials) for the Avatar API / image-error path — that is not the same as teaching the fallback look
- Reserve fallback-only Avatars for pages or examples whose **job** is to show missing/broken image behavior (Avatar / AvatarGroup surface docs)

## Do not

- Ship list rows, pickers, or groups with initials-only faces when a photo would work
- Invent random CDN hosts when `mockmind-api.uifaces.co` already matches DS preview fixtures
- Omit `fallback` to “hide” it — the prop stays required; the visual teaching point is the photo

## Live demos vs fences

- Live demos (`src/components/demos/**`): real `src` + real names
- MDX fences: keep `src` on Avatar when the fence teaches item addons / people rows; do not strip `src` to shorten the fence
